\details{
Collects named data frames from supported \code{mfrmr} objects or their
\code{summary()} outputs into \code{tables}, indexed by \code{table_index} (dimensions,
appendix roles, descriptions) and \code{plot_index} (numeric views). G-study,
D-study, D-study comparison, residual-network, and \code{mfrm_report()} inputs
retain complete signed/unavailable evidence rows without \code{top_n} truncation,
while fit, diagnostics, recovery, calibration, and model-choice summaries
preserve their role-classified caveat, \code{reading_order}, \code{population_coding},
and df-sensitivity tables for \code{\link[=apa_table]{apa_table()}} and \code{\link[=export_summary_appendix]{export_summary_appendix()}}.

This method provides a compact summary for bundle-like outputs
(for example: unexpected-response, fair-average, chi-square, and
category report objects). It extracts:
\itemize{
\item object class and available components
\item one-row summary table when available
\item preview rows from the main data component
\item resolved settings/options
}

Branch-aware summaries are provided for:
\itemize{
\item \code{mfrm_bias_count} (\code{branch = "original"} / \code{"facets"})
\item \code{mfrm_fixed_reports} (\code{branch = "original"} / \code{"facets"})
\item \code{mfrm_visual_summaries} (\code{branch = "original"} / \code{"facets"})
}

Additional class-aware summaries are provided for:
\itemize{
\item \code{mfrm_unexpected}, \code{mfrm_fair_average}, \code{mfrm_displacement}
\item \code{mfrm_interrater}, \code{mfrm_facets_chisq}, \code{mfrm_bias_interaction}
\item \code{mfrm_rating_scale}, \code{mfrm_category_structure}, \code{mfrm_category_curves}
\item \code{mfrm_measurable}, \code{mfrm_unexpected_after_bias}, \code{mfrm_output_bundle}
\item \code{mfrm_residual_pca}, \code{mfrm_specifications}, \code{mfrm_data_quality},
\code{mfrm_fit_measures}
\item \code{mfrm_iteration_report}, \code{mfrm_subset_connectivity}, \code{mfrm_facet_statistics}
\item \code{mfrm_facets_contract_review}, \code{mfrm_facets_fit_review},
\code{mfrm_facets_fit_df_guide}, \code{mfrm_reference_benchmark}
}

\code{plot()} dispatches by bundle class:
\itemize{
\item \code{mfrm_unexpected} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "unexpected")}
\item \code{mfrm_fair_average} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "fair_average")}
\item \code{mfrm_displacement} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "displacement")}
\item \code{mfrm_interrater} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "agreement")}
\item \code{mfrm_facets_chisq} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "facets_chisq")}
\item \code{mfrm_bias_interaction} -> \link[=plot.mfrm_fit]{plot(x, type = "bias")}
\item \code{mfrm_bias_count} -> bias-count plots (cell counts / low-count rates)
\item \code{mfrm_fixed_reports} -> pairwise-contrast diagnostics
\item \code{mfrm_visual_summaries} -> warning/summary message count plots
\item \code{mfrm_category_structure} -> category count and boundary plots
\item \code{mfrm_category_curves} -> overview (default), ogive, CCC / category
probability / conditional probability, cumulative, total-information, and
category-specific-information plots
\item \code{mfrm_rating_scale} -> category-counts/threshold plots
\item \code{mfrm_measurable} -> measurable-data coverage/count plots
\item \code{mfrm_unexpected_after_bias} -> post-bias unexpected-response plots
\item \code{mfrm_output_bundle} -> graph/score output-file diagnostics,
including \code{type = "score_se"} when scorefile SE columns are available
\item \code{mfrm_residual_pca} -> residual PCA scree, parallel-analysis, or
